    "body": "Militaries around the globe have been studying the Ukraine and Iran conflicts to learn about the impacts of missile technologies, drones and air defense systems. But every conflict is different, and every region has different needs.\nTo understand what lessons are and are not applicable in different parts of the world, Becca Wasser of Bloomberg Economics and Mark Cancian of the Center for International and Strategic Studies joined Breaking Defense Editor-in-Chief Aaron Mehta for this new roundtable video.\nKeep an eye on future episodes here , and catch part one here .\nBreaking Defense Video\nThe real-world missile defense lessons from Ukraine and Iran — and how they matter for China\nWatch Now »\nA $1.1 trillion Pentagon budget plan sets up a fight on Capitol Hill\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon fails another audit. Can it turn things around by 2028?\nWatch Now »\nA new Air Force stunt plane, plus a shakeup for special operations\nWatch Now »\nNATO nations have a missile crisis. How did it happen, and can it be fixed?\nWatch Now »\nA Pentagon impeachment showdown, plus defense funding in limbo\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe push to give dismounted forces direct access to LEO and MEO networks [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon wants a massive new military base. Where will it go?\nWatch Now »\nWhat now? Budget fight, Hegseth impeachment on deck for defense-focused lawmakers after midterms\nWatch Now »\nThe defense show circuit keeps rolling, plus Jimmy Stewart goes to war\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
